findings.comment:
750.800b - The following food contact surfaces were soiled:
A) can opener blade (food debris) - placed through ware washing cycle in the dish machine during inspection;
B) soda gun holder at bar (mold) - placed through ware washing cycle in the dish machine during inspection;   and;
C) inside small ice machine - around baffle & in upper filter/ice tray area (mold).

Clean and sanitize food contact surfaces between uses/as needed, up to every 4hrs after continuous use, to prevent cross contamination and eliminate buildup of debris.

750.800e - The following non-food contact surfaces were soiled:
A) walkin cooler - inverted crates and shelving (mold);
B) lower shelves used for storage of covered plates and onions (dust);
C) sprayer surface (mold in crevice);
D) shelving at prep table in kitchen (both sides with food debris/general buildup)
E) tub with sharpies and labels in kitchen (food debris);
F) oven drip trays (food debris);
G) shelving in side kitchen and salt/pepper shaker storage tub (food debris/splash);
H) inside keg cooler at banquet room bar (buildup).

Clean non-food contact surfaces daily/as needed to eliminate buildup of debris.

findings.citation_text:
750.1220 - Floors were observed to be soiled in the following areas;
A) dry storage under shelving (dust/insect/debris);
B) along the floor to wall juncture under the dish area (general buildup);
C) under/behind cooking equipment in the kitchen (grease/food debris);   and
D) under cooler in kitchen (debris/dust).

Floors shall be kept clean. Clean the floors throughout under equipment and along walls daily/as needed to eliminate buildup of debris.

